  "changes": [
    "Large UTF-8 slices share one flat source owner; slices below 256 B or retaining more than twice their size copy. Nested views flatten.",
    "Views preserve native strong-count/length offsets, carry no ASCII hint and cannot append in place. Native inline-byte readers retain their checked paths.",
    "For view roots below 1 MiB, regex subjects share the flat prepared element/offset tables. Matchers receive only the visible element range; indices remain relative UTF-16 units.",
    "Existing string/regex cache budgets charge full retained owners and tables. Identity-aware memory census deduplicates shared roots and prepared parents."
  ],
